ACCEPT — PR #20239 at head `e6737d70a7` · `domain:spec` seat 2 (`session_01QcAS3qiYYZNezaxZxaUdMV`) · 2026-09-27T13:23Z

Seat review against GitHub, not the report:
- **Shape:** draft, base `main`, `Fixes #20026` and `Clause-②: no` line-leading. 3 files, +65/−30: `validation.zod.ts`, `validation.test.ts` and one `patch` changeset.
  - The PR had no assignee: the resume order's "no label writes" also withheld the assignee write. The seat sets `os-project-manager` in this act.
- **Delivered, under the seat's scope correction** (the card's title says every example predicate, and the claim's surface is the whole docblock above `ConditionalValidationSchema`):
  - all 19 predicates in Use Cases 1–7 and on the ObjectStack side of the Salesforce comparison are rewritten in CEL (`record.FIELD == VALUE`, `&&`, `||`, `matches`);
  - the Salesforce-formula side is left as it was;
  - the `validation.zod.ts` hunks are comment lines only (measured: no `+`/`-` line outside ` * `);
  - the seven matching test fixtures moved with the examples.
- **Evidence (the report's):**
  - `ExpressionEngine.evaluate` gives 20/20 as expected on true and false records;
  - the lit control shows all 19 old strings still fail;
  - the dist d.ts carries each new string ×1 and each old string ×0;
  - spec build, `check:generated`, the validation tests (72/72) and typecheck are green.
- **Out-of-scope finding:** `content/docs/protocol/objectql/index.mdx:186` → Acceptance notes. It is already recorded in `docs/audits/2026-06-handwritten-docs-accuracy-followups.md`, and no reach was measured.
- **Next:** at-tier contract review of this head. The path limb fires on `packages/spec/src/data/validation.zod.ts` (TSDoc only), and the review must judge each rewritten predicate: in particular, the escaping of the `matches` pattern as a copied TS string literal. `needs:contract-review` goes on the PR in this act.
